# The power mode of a device, from its battery, its heat and the frames it drops: the first holding row decides
law power_mode
kind table
claim a device that is hot, or nearly out of battery, runs in the minimal mode
claim a device with a low battery, a warm device, and one that drops frames, run in the standard mode; every other device runs in the full mode
claim the rows are tried from the top, so a hot device with an empty battery is decided by `hot`
source the rule is stated here (nothing outside this file defines it)

x-input battery_pct integer
x-input thermal text
x-input frame_drops integer

const empty_below integer = 15
const low_below integer = 30
const dropping_from integer = 10

value full standard minimal
row hot: minimal when thermal == "serious" or thermal == "critical"
row empty: minimal when battery_pct < empty_below
row low: standard when battery_pct < low_below
row warm: standard when thermal == "fair"
row dropping: standard when frame_drops >= dropping_from
otherwise full

verdict the mode and the row that gave it, for every combination of the values the rows compare with
